  :adr/decision-summary
  "{:trigger \"owner asked to bring num/torch/comfyui-clj to ComfyUI-py/PyTorch-equivalent maturity, same session that fixed+sped up the real Python ComfyUI on the murakumo fleet\",
    :measured-gap {:num-lines 744 :torch-lines 626 :comfyui-clj-lines 1309
                   :real-comfyui-py-lines 239926
                   :note \"PyTorch's own ATen/MPS kernel library not counted — multi-million-line C++/CUDA/Metal, ~1000x gap total, not a single-ADR task\"},
    :correction {:prior-claim \"num Metal backend S2/unimplemented, CPU+WGSL-reference only\"
                :actual (str \"WRONG — verify/metal_contract.js: 13/13 BLAS ops verified on real Apple M4 Metal via wgpu; \"
                              \"verify/metal_pcg.js: real Jacobi-PCG Poisson solver converges on-GPU. num ADR-0001 S1+S3 already done. \"
                              \"Actual gap: no conv2d kernel, no torch<->num wiring, num's own S2 (native MPS fast-path) unstarted.\")},
    :phase1-in [\"num.wgsl conv2d kernel (CPU-reference + contract test + live-Metal verification, same rigor as existing 13)\"
                \"torch.num-backend implementing torch.ports/IBackend for :linear :relu :conv2d :softmax\"
                \"correctness: f32-tolerance match vs num.cpu oracle for a small fixed model\"
                \"honest benchmark: num-Metal forward pass vs real PyTorch MPS on the murakumo fleet, same shapes\"],
    :phase1-out [\"attention/transformer ops, U-Net-scale architecture, diffusion samplers, safetensors loading, any SDXL-class model\"
                 \"autograd/training (forward-pass inference only)\"
                 \"num's own S2 native Apple MPS-API fast path\"
                 \"kotoba-lang/comfyui reimplementation (stays HTTP-orchestrating real Python ComfyUI via murakumo, unchanged)\"
                 \"any claim of PyTorch/ComfyUI maturity parity on completion\"],
    :not-urgent \"real diffusion-model inference speed already solved pragmatically this session (murakumo fix: ComfyUI 0.27.0 upgrade + dead-node detection + LaunchDaemon self-heal, ~3min/image on Metal/MPS, all 8 fleet nodes) — Phase 1 is a parallel foundation investment, not blocking anything\",
    :implementation-status \"NOT started — this ADR is the scope fence only, a future session picks up the actual work\"}"}]
